tool_settings.uv_peel.world_space=World Density
tool_settings.uv_peel.world_space_tooltip=Use one tile per 64 displayed map units along the guide before Repeat and Offset. Quad strips normalize transverse lanes to the widest span. Turn off to fit each guide and its transverse span to one tile; the guide stays at the offset and opposite sides use opposite signs.
tool_settings.uv_peel.u_repeat=U Repeat
tool_settings.uv_peel.v_repeat=V Repeat
tool_settings.uv_peel.u_offset=U Offset (tiles)
tool_settings.uv_peel.v_offset=V Offset (tiles)
tool_settings.uv_peel.help=Selected edges guide U or V texture flow. Peel walks across successive quads on both sides, including around corners, until a boundary, non-quad face, or closed circuit. One edge can map an entire strip. Separate guides can overwrite overlapping strips.
ui.standard_material_editor.texture_transform.tooltip=Shared material transform: affects every texture channel and every surface using this material, after face UV mapping.
ui.standard_material_editor.texture_transform.center.tooltip=Pivot for material UV tiling and rotation, measured in texture tiles. The default 0.5, 0.5 is the image center.
ui.standard_material_editor.texture_transform.scale.tooltip=Multiply material UV repetitions. Larger magnitudes make the texture smaller; negative values mirror it. Applies to every surface using this material.
ui.standard_material_editor.texture_transform.offset.tooltip=Offset the material UV coordinates in texture tiles after tiling and rotation. One unit equals a full texture tile.
ui.standard_material_editor.texture_transform.rotation.tooltip=Rotate material UV coordinates around Center, after tiling and before Offset. Applies to every surface using this material.
tool_settings.texture_scale_x.tooltip=Texture width (U) scale; its screen direction follows the mapped texture. Larger magnitudes enlarge the texture; negative values mirror it. Authored UVs and material tiling also affect visible density.
tool_settings.texture_scale_y.tooltip=Texture height (V) scale; its screen direction follows the mapped texture. Larger magnitudes enlarge the texture; negative values mirror it. Authored UVs and material tiling also affect visible density.
tool_settings.texture_shift_x.tooltip=Shift along the texture image's width axis (U), in image pixels. Its screen direction follows the mapped texture. Numeric shifts require one selected face.
tool_settings.texture_shift_y.tooltip=Shift along the texture image's height axis (V), in image pixels. Its screen direction follows the mapped texture. Numeric shifts require one selected face.
tool_settings.texture_rotate.tooltip=Texture rotation in degrees in the face's upright planar projection. Selecting the face again preserves its angle. Other mappings retain their face rotation setting.
tool_settings.uv_peel.u_repeat.tooltip=Multiply U repetitions after World Density or per-patch normalization. Larger values make the texture smaller.
tool_settings.uv_peel.v_repeat.tooltip=Multiply V repetitions after World Density or per-patch normalization. Larger values make the texture smaller.
tool_settings.uv_peel.u_offset.tooltip=Shift the generated U coordinates in texture tiles after Repeat. One unit equals a full texture tile.
tool_settings.uv_peel.v_offset.tooltip=Shift the generated V coordinates in texture tiles after Repeat. One unit equals a full texture tile.
tool_settings.edit_texture.align_to_grid.tooltip=Project on world axes and reset scale to 0.125 map units per texel, rotation to zero, and shifts to zero.
tool_settings.edit_texture.align_to_face.tooltip=Project on the face plane while retaining scale, rotation, and shifts. The texture origin moves to a face corner.
tool_settings.edit_texture.align_to_view.tooltip=Project using the captured view axes while retaining scale, rotation, and shifts. Angled surfaces can appear stretched.
tool_settings.edit_texture.scale_x_up.tooltip=Double texture width (U) by doubling the face scale magnitude. Retain its mirror sign.
tool_settings.edit_texture.scale_x_down.tooltip=Halve texture width (U) by halving the face scale magnitude. Retain its mirror sign.
tool_settings.edit_texture.scale_y_up.tooltip=Double texture height (V) by doubling the face scale magnitude. Retain its mirror sign.
tool_settings.edit_texture.scale_y_down.tooltip=Halve texture height (V) by halving the face scale magnitude. Retain its mirror sign.
tool_settings.edit_texture.shift_left.tooltip=Move the texture left by one image pixel along its texture axis, accounting for rotation and mirroring.
tool_settings.edit_texture.shift_right.tooltip=Move the texture right by one image pixel along its texture axis, accounting for rotation and mirroring.
tool_settings.edit_texture.shift_up.tooltip=Move the texture up by one image pixel along its texture axis, accounting for rotation and mirroring.
tool_settings.edit_texture.shift_down.tooltip=Move the texture down by one image pixel along its texture axis, accounting for rotation and mirroring.
tool_settings.edit_texture.rotate_clockwise.tooltip=Rotate the texture image clockwise by the current rotation step, viewed from the face front.
tool_settings.edit_texture.rotate_counter_clockwise.tooltip=Rotate the texture image counterclockwise by the current rotation step, viewed from the face front.
tool_settings.edit_texture.flip_texture_horizontal.tooltip=Mirror the texture along its width axis (U) about its chart origin. Keep the current shifts.
tool_settings.edit_texture.flip_texture_vertical.tooltip=Mirror the texture along its height axis (V) about its chart origin. Keep the current shifts.
tool_settings.edit_texture.flip_face_horizontal.tooltip=Mirror the face UVs along U within their existing bounds. Treat as One uses combined UV bounds across the selection. Geometry and scalar texture settings stay unchanged.
tool_settings.edit_texture.flip_face_vertical.tooltip=Mirror the face UVs along V within their existing bounds. Treat as One uses combined UV bounds across the selection. Geometry and scalar texture settings stay unchanged.
tool_settings.edit_texture.fit_both.tooltip=Scale and shift both texture axes to fit one tile to the face bounds. Treat as One uses shared projection and combined bounds.
tool_settings.edit_texture.fit_x.tooltip=Scale and shift the texture width axis (U) to fit one tile. Keep the V mapping. Treat as One uses a shared projection.
tool_settings.edit_texture.fit_y.tooltip=Scale and shift the texture height axis (V) to fit one tile. Keep the U mapping. Treat as One uses a shared projection.
tool_settings.edit_texture.justify_left.tooltip=Shift the texture to the left bound without scaling each face. Treat as One can change density through its shared projection.
tool_settings.edit_texture.justify_right.tooltip=Shift the texture to the right bound without scaling each face. Treat as One can change density through its shared projection.
tool_settings.edit_texture.justify_top.tooltip=Shift the texture to the top bound without scaling each face. Treat as One can change density through its shared projection.
tool_settings.edit_texture.justify_bottom.tooltip=Shift the texture to the bottom bound without scaling each face. Treat as One can change density through its shared projection.
tool_settings.edit_texture.justify_center.tooltip=Center the texture within the face bounds without scaling. Treat as One can change density through its shared projection.
