viewport.tool.uv_peel.label=Guided UV Peel
tool_settings.target.uv_peel=Guided UV Peel
tool_settings.description.uv_peel=Activate the tool, select edge guides, adjust the live preview, then Apply or Cancel. Selected edges guide U or V texture flow. Peel walks across successive quads on both sides, including around corners, until a boundary, non-quad face, or closed circuit. One edge can map an entire strip. Separate guides can overwrite overlapping strips.
uv_peel.world_space.tooltip=Use one tile per 64 displayed map units along the guide before Repeat and Offset. Quad strips normalize transverse lanes to the widest span. Turn off to fit each guide and its transverse span to one tile; the guide stays at the offset and opposite sides use opposite signs.
uv_peel.u_repeat.tooltip=Multiply U repetitions after World Density or per-patch normalization. Larger values make the texture smaller.
uv_peel.v_repeat.tooltip=Multiply V repetitions after World Density or per-patch normalization. Larger values make the texture smaller.
uv_peel.u_offset.tooltip=Shift the generated U coordinates in texture tiles after Repeat. One unit equals a full texture tile.
uv_peel.v_offset.tooltip=Shift the generated V coordinates in texture tiles after Repeat. One unit equals a full texture tile.
